      "id": 1,
      "text": "Redstone was founded in 1889 by John Cleveland Osgood, who began building a vast coal and steel empire.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.achp.gov/preserve-america/community/redstone-colorado"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Osgood built 84 cottages and a 40‑room inn, all with indoor plumbing and electricity, for his miners and cokers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redstone%2C_Colorado"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Tudor‑style Cleveholm Manor, later called Redstone Castle, was completed in 1901 and still houses 75% of its original furnishings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redstone%2C_Colorado"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Redstone’s historic district, listed on the National Register, includes several separately listed properties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redstone%2C_Colorado"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Near the historic coke ovens off CO‑133, a trailhead opens to over five miles of single‑track trails looping through the area.",
